    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0264" n="172" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg172"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1501</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-22T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 24, 4.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2919. Person referred to in my 2769, March 4,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d109-f1"/>
                    contemplates returning home in a few days. Is there any message the Department
                    desires to have intimated to him unofficially?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
